**Definition 7.2 (fixed successful control path).** Every handoff below
is the actual named TOK followed by its finite CTL. Bank assignments
remain fully expanded as in Definition 2.1.

| Entry | Operation and successor |
| --- | --- |
| ClientImage | Position/import73; run inherited full Image/binding checks; build $b_*$ from that acquired target. ACK Image and return mailbox availability. Keep the flight's invocation, with no M append/Ready. Transfer client→handler and enter RenderS. |
| RenderS | Use only the acquired Image's raw projection to emit S. Clear acquired Image work fields. Publish stage0 and enter CheckS0. |
| CheckS0 | Position73, clear candidate, import actual stage0 to received, parse body into sourceBody, independently run $D_S$/re-encoding/binding checks. Save this received body as firstS. ACK/mailbox return; client→handler; FromS. |
| FromS / CheckB | Compute B solely from sourceBody; publish stage1. CheckB positions/imports73 after clearing candidate; independently checks B and binding; ACK/mailbox return; transfer to FromB. |
| FromB / CheckM | Compute M solely from received B; publish stage2. CheckM independently imports/checks the actual M; ACK/mailbox return; transfer to FromM. |
| FromM / CheckT | Compute T solely from received M; publish stage3. CheckT independently imports/checks actual T; ACK/mailbox return; transfer to FromT. |
| FromT / CheckS1 | Compute S solely from received T; publish stage4. CheckS1 independently imports/decodes/checks actual final S and compares it with firstS. Serialize its own decoded prefix/raw record as HistoricalImage and run the original ClientImage value-checker subgraph on that value. |
| FinalReturn | ACK final channel exactly once; return mailbox availability; append one complete five-field GCA history item, including actual mode/frame, typed outcome and received-reference bindings; return invocation to outer client; execute the sole final Ready. |

No later arrow reads the initial Image. firstS is read only for the
final equality comparison. All callback candidates are cleared before
actual import; sourceBody is assigned only from that import. There is
no repair or implicit input branch. The original checker in CheckS1
does not repeat an ACK: it is CYCLE's CheckImageValue parser/check
subgraph, with the final ACK in FinalReturn.

The successful five-field completed item is exactly
`[choice,mode,wholeFrame,outcome,receivedBindings]`. Its last field is
the ordered eight-item list for CoverRef, PackageRef, Image, then
View0 through View4. Each item is the already acquired complete
binding header from that actual imported tuple: the complete CoverRef
and PackageRef tuples; the Image tuple with only its final Image value
removed; and each View tuple with only its final natural body removed.
Thus all service/source/cover/package/target fields and the static View
stage/tag remain. Complete origins inside those fields retain their
inherited grammars, not just their ordinals. Current receiver placement,
copy and completion origins remain in the actual channel material and
native history; this list does not invent a receiver's future origin
inside its own sent word.
Append that record at its callback by actual word operations. Typed
rejections instead retain the ordered list of bindings actually received
on that rejection route. The completed-item parser requires five fields,
then parses this list by outcome/kind; reservoir recovery uses only the
mode and whole-frame fields. The decoder/arrow work-clear preserves
this list as a service field, but no arrow reads it as a logical input.
FinalReturn writes it only after the final value check and ACK.

